From: lxx0329 <lxx0329@noreply.atomgit.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0005] ohos: degrade fdinfo-open failure to unknown count (-fc disabled)

The -fc trigger counts file descriptors by opendir("/proc/<pid>/fdinfo").
On OHOS (non-root, restricted procfs) that directory is not readable by an
unprivileged monitor, so upstream logs an error and GetProcessStat() returns
false, aborting monitoring entirely -- even for -c/-m triggers that never
need the fd count. Treat the failed open as an unknown count (-1) instead:
-fc never fires on an unknown count (num_fd >= threshold is false), and all
other triggers keep working. Root hosts and readable procfs behave unchanged.

Note: fddir is declared auto_free_dir, so cleanup_dir() closes it exactly once
on every return path; closing it explicitly here as well made closedir() run
twice on the same DIR (double close of the fd + double free of the DIR buffer),
which crashes the first CpuMonitoringThread poll inside libc.
---
--- a/src/Process.c
+++ b/src/Process.c
@@ -36,15 +36,19 @@
         {
             proc->num_filedescriptors++;
         }
+        proc->num_filedescriptors-=2;               // Account for "." and ".."
     }
     else
     {
-        Log(error, "Failed to open %s. Exiting...", procFilePath);
-        return false;
-
-    }
-
-    proc->num_filedescriptors-=2;                   // Account for "." and ".."
+        // OHOS non-root procfs restriction (and any system that hides
+        // /proc/<pid>/fdinfo from unprivileged readers): the fd count is
+        // only consumed by the -fc trigger (Monitor.c), so do not abort the
+        // whole monitor over it. Mark the count unknown (-1); -fc then never
+        // fires (num_fd >= threshold is false), while -c/-m/-cl/-ml/ondemand
+        // triggers keep working from /proc/<pid>/stat and friends.
+        Trace("WARNING: Failed to open %s; fd count unknown (-fc disabled)", procFilePath);
+        proc->num_filedescriptors = -1;
+    }
 
 
     // Read /proc/[pid]/stat
